cation S.O. 5319(E), 2025","documentType":"Official Gazette notification","official":true,"reviewStatus":"needs-legal-review","officialUrl":"https://www.labour.gov.in/","fileName":"social-security-code-commencement-so-5319e-2025.pdf","drivePath":"GrowWithHR-RAG/01-source-documents/official/social-security/03-notifications/social-security-code-commencement-so-5319e-2025.pdf","sha256":"014ba41eba2c0beda344bf084e1bed1d6f7f6929aabdbc7b4fa25fe22bce45c5","byteLength":408295,"pageCount":2},{"registrySourceId":"social-security-code-corrigendum-so-5936e-2025","title":"Code on Social Security corrigendum S.O. 5936(E), 2025","documentType":"Official Gazette corrigendum","official":true,"reviewStatus":"needs-legal-review","officialUrl":"https://www.labour.gov.in/whats-new","fileName":"social-security-code-corrigendum-so-5936e-2025.pdf","drivePath":"GrowWithHR-RAG/01-source-documents/official/social-security/03-notifications/social-security-code-corrigendum-so-5936e-2025.pdf","sha256":"d14b088ef05a8f34c37d823b3b6fc6bd78a101e37882edc256d931e01e063a03","byteLength":560515,"pageCount":2}],"chunks":[{"chunkId":"esi-code-establishment-wave4a-001","registrySourceId":"social-security-code-2020","title":"ESI establishment and coverage-route framework","sectionReference":"Section 1, selected section 2 definitions and First Schedule Chapter IV","pageStart":8,"pageEnd":19,"priority":100,"reasonCodes":["ESI_ESTABLISHMENT_CONTROLS_RECORDED_SPECIALIST_REVIEW","ESI_ESTABLISHMENT_CONTROL_GAPS_SPECIALIST_REVIEW","ESI_ESTABLISHMENT_FACTS_MISSING"],"retrievalTerms":["establishment","coverage route","registration","branches"],"text":"The controlled Code source provides central establishment and Chapter IV routing context. Wave 4A records a declared route and organisation controls but does not decide coverage, thresholds, special routes or area commencement.","contentSha256":"184296b630a0aa987ea7b038bca50ddbd908a7aef82ecf285bc3616ee146be14"},{"chunkId":"esi-central-rules-registration-wave4a-001","registrySourceId":"social-security-central-rules-2026","title":"Current central registration and insurance-process context","sectionReference":"Rules 1–5 and Rule 18","pageStart":135,"pageEnd":159,"priority":100,"reasonCodes":["ESI_ESTABLISHMENT_CONTROLS_RECORDED_SPECIALIST_REVIEW","ESI_ESTABLISHMENT_CONTROL_GAPS_SPECIALIST_REVIEW","ESI_ESTABLISHMENT_FACTS_MISSING","ESI_EMPLOYEE_INSURANCE_CONTROLS_RECORDED_SPECIALIST_REVIEW","ESI_EMPLOYEE_INSURANCE_CONTROL_GAPS_SPECIALIST_REVIEW","ESI_EMPLOYEE_INSURANCE_FACTS_MISSING"],"retrievalTerms":["registration","voluntary route","employee insurance","declaration"],"text":"The controlled Central Rules source provides current central registration and employee-insurance process context. The route does not accept identity records or determine whether any individual is insured.","contentSha256":"a42d9e4fd5894a02a9f7e010feaca2bcf88c1ea10ca05d47697534c9ac4bc26f"},{"chunkId":"esi-general-regulations-registration-wave4a-001","registrySourceId":"employees-state-insurance-general-regulations-1950","title":"Saved-law registration and identity-process context","sectionReference":"Regulations 10-B to 17-B","pageStart":7,"pageEnd":9,"priority":100,"reasonCodes":["ESI_ESTABLISHMENT_CONTROLS_RECORDED_SPECIALIST_REVIEW","ESI_ESTABLISHMENT_CONTROL_GAPS_SPECIALIST_REVIEW","ESI_ESTABLISHMENT_FACTS_MISSING","ESI_EMPLOYEE_INSURANCE_CONTROLS_RECORDED_SPECIALIST_REVIEW","ESI_EMPLOYEE_INSURANCE_CONTROL_GAPS_SPECIALIST_REVIEW","ESI_EMPLOYEE_INSURANCE_FACTS_MISSING"],"retrievalTerms":["registration","insurance number","declaration","saved law"],"text":"The consolidated General Regulations are retained only as a saved-law candidate for operational registration context. Their prospective use and transition treatment require qualified legal review.","contentSha256":"55585546789c5ac82febe99af2a8ece6212256329efd0459d0fbb07ee895eacf"},{"chunkId":"esi-code-contractor-payment-wave4a-001","registrySourceId":"social-security-code-2020","title":"Principal-employer and contribution-control framework","sectionReference":"Sections 29–31","pageStart":31,"pageEnd":35,"priority":100,"reasonCodes":["ESI_CONTRACTOR_CONTROLS_RECORDED_SPECIALIST_REVIEW","ESI_CONTRACTOR_CONTROL_GAPS_SPECIALIST_REVIEW","ESI_CONTRACTOR_FACTS_MISSING","ESI_PAYMENT_CONTROLS_RECORDED_SPECIALIST_REVIEW","ESI_PAYMENT_CONTROL_GAPS_SPECIALIST_REVIEW","ESI_PAYMENT_FACTS_MISSING"],"retrievalTerms":["principal employer","immediate employer","contribution","payment"],"text":"The controlled Code source provides principal-employer, contractor and contribution responsibility context. Wave 4A reviews controls only and does not calculate contributions or determine liability in a dispute.","contentSha256":"59e5d3e0681116dd45e7de021c2540600ef46d3c61787f4c7230bceaf3854787"},{"chunkId":"esi-general-regulations-contractor-payment-wave4a-001","registrySourceId":"employees-state-insurance-general-regulations-1950","title":"Saved-law contractor, payment and return-process context","sectionReference":"Regulations 26–40","pageStart":10,"pageEnd":12,"priority":100,"reasonCodes":["ESI_CONTRACTOR_CONTROLS_RECORDED_SPECIALIST_REVIEW","ESI_CONTRACTOR_CONTROL_GAPS_SPECIALIST_REVIEW","ESI_CONTRACTOR_FACTS_MISSING","ESI_PAYMENT_CONTROLS_RECORDED_SPECIALIST_REVIEW","ESI_PAYMENT_CONTROL_GAPS_SPECIALIST_REVIEW","ESI_PAYMENT_FACTS_MISSING"],"retrievalTerms":["contractor register","reconciliation","remittance","return filing"],"text":"The consolidated General Regulations provide candidate operational context for registers, reconciliation, payment and returns. Saved-law treatment, current due dates, forms and portal processes remain unresolved.","contentSha256":"83dfbe386c362c6206984a3c19df61457400cfc993152ce64fb99050766b4446"},{"chunkId":"esi-central-rules-payment-wave4a-001","registrySourceId":"social-security-central-rules-2026","title":"Current ordinary contribution framework","sectionReference":"Rule 19","pageStart":159,"pageEnd":160,"priority":100,"reasonCodes":["ESI_PAYMENT_CONTROLS_RECORDED_SPECIALIST_REVIEW","ESI_PAYMENT_CONTROL_GAPS_SPECIALIST_REVIEW","ESI_PAYMENT_FACTS_MISSING"],"retrievalTerms":["ordinary contribution","employer share","employee share","rate source"],"text":"Rule 19 is retained as current central contribution framework context. Wave 4A does not expose rate values, select an applicable rate, accept wage amounts or perform arithmetic.","contentSha256":"4fea9fe63485b9ca7038d29aca964988629ecca4a0459e28eb4adf366704abcf"},{"chunkId":"esi-central-rules-legacy-wave4a-001","registrySourceId":"employees-state-insurance-central-rules-1950","title":"Historical ESI Central Rules context","sectionReference":"Consolidated historical rules","pageStart":1,"pageEnd":32,"priority":100,"reasonCodes":["ESI_ESTABLISHMENT_CONTROLS_RECORDED_SPECIALIST_REVIEW","ESI_ESTABLISHMENT_CONTROL_GAPS_SPECIALIST_REVIEW","ESI_ESTABLISHMENT_FACTS_MISSING","ESI_PAYMENT_CONTROLS_RECORDED_SPECIALIST_REVIEW","ESI_PAYMENT_CONTROL_GAPS_SPECIALIST_REVIEW","ESI_PAYMENT_FACTS_MISSING"],"retrievalTerms":["historical rules","transition","registration","contribution"],"text":"The consolidated 1950 Central Rules are retained only as historical and transition context. They are not represented as prospective current authority for thresholds, rates, due dates or coverage.","contentSha256":"17dff6191cb77b0e52fd7e5426ecdb49605d67aac457b5c63d9018629e4bf1ae"},{"chunkId":"esi-code-accident-wave4a-001","registrySourceId":"social-security-code-2020","title":"Employment-injury and accident-control framework","sectionReference":"Sections 34–38","pageStart":35,"pageEnd":40,"priority":100,"reasonCodes":["ESI_ACCIDENT_CONTROLS_RECORDED_SPECIALIST_REVIEW","ESI_ACCIDENT_CONTROL_GAPS_SPECIALIST_REVIEW","ESI_ACCIDENT_FACTS_MISSING"],"retrievalTerms":["employment injury","accident reporting","register","escalation"],"text":"The controlled Code source provides employment-injury and accident-control context. Wave 4A does not process accident narratives or determine causation, injury classification or benefit entitlement.","contentSha256":"604f20984ace21aa67fc65d56f7b3cc09c016a70e6873daca9ee4da92f0d1ba5"},{"chunkId":"esi-general-regulations-accident-wave4a-001","registrySourceId":"employees-state-insurance-general-regulations-1950","title":"Saved-law accident-book and reporting context","sectionReference":"Regulations 65–76-A","pageStart":17,"pageEnd":20,"priority":100,"reasonCodes":["ESI_ACCIDENT_CONTROLS_RECORDED_SPECIALIST_REVIEW","ESI_ACCIDENT_CONTROL_GAPS_SPECIALIST_REVIEW","ESI_ACCIDENT_FACTS_MISSING"],"retrievalTerms":["accident book","serious accident","reporting","saved law"],"text":"The consolidated General Regulations are retained as a saved-law candidate for accident-book and reporting-process context. Current forms, timing and report sufficiency require specialist verification.","contentSha256":"23bd4daae3014147c62da4d263bc3a5f63b86a37b22ed278c0c8f9dd36fad4c1"},{"chunkId":"esi-commencement-wave4a-001","registrySourceId":"social-security-code-commencement-so-5319e-2025","title":"Commencement and transition context","sectionReference":"S.O. 5319(E), dated 21 November 2025","pageStart":1,"pageEnd":2,"priority":100,"reasonCodes":["ESI_ESTABLISHMENT_CONTROLS_RECORDED_SPECIALIST_REVIEW","ESI_ESTABLISHMENT_CONTROL_GAPS_SPECIALIST_REVIEW","ESI_ESTABLISHMENT_FACTS_MISSING","ESI_EMPLOYEE_INSURANCE_CONTROLS_RECORDED_SPECIALIST_REVIEW","ESI_EMPLOYEE_INSURANCE_CONTROL_GAPS_SPECIALIST_REVIEW","ESI_EMPLOYEE_INSURANCE_FACTS_MISSING","ESI_CONTRACTOR_CONTROLS_RECORDED_SPECIALIST_REVIEW","ESI_CONTRACTOR_CONTROL_GAPS_SPECIALIST_REVIEW","ESI_CONTRACTOR_FACTS_MISSING","ESI_PAYMENT_CONTROLS_RECORDED_SPECIALIST_REVIEW","ESI_PAYMENT_CONTROL_GAPS_SPECIALIST_REVIEW","ESI_PAYMENT_FACTS_MISSING","ESI_ACCIDENT_CONTROLS_RECORDED_SPECIALIST_REVIEW","ESI_ACCIDENT_CONTROL_GAPS_SPECIALIST_REVIEW","ESI_ACCIDENT_FACTS_MISSING"],"retrievalTerms":["commencement","Chapter IV","transition","saved law"],"text":"The controlled commencement notification is retained as effective-date context. Area commencement, legacy-instrument savings and operational transition questions cannot be resolved by retrieval or provider output.","contentSha256":"c7ffa40414084805f92129cd38651413258ce1bc250b4819198afbd9474e1278"},{"chunkId":"esi-corrigendum-wave4a-001","registrySourceId":"social-security-code-corrigendum-so-5936e-2025","title":"Corrigendum context","sectionReference":"S.O. 5936(E), dated 19 December 2025","pageStart":1,"pageEnd":2,"priority":100,"reasonCodes":["ESI_ESTABLISHMENT_CONTROLS_RECORDED_SPECIALIST_REVIEW","ESI_ESTABLISHMENT_CONTROL_GAPS_SPECIALIST_REVIEW","ESI_ESTABLISHMENT_FACTS_MISSING","ESI_EMPLOYEE_INSURANCE_CONTROLS_RECORDED_SPECIALIST_REVIEW","ESI_EMPLOYEE_INSURANCE_CONTROL_GAPS_SPECIALIST_REVIEW","ESI_EMPLOYEE_INSURANCE_FACTS_MISSING","ESI_CONTRACTOR_CONTROLS_RECORDED_SPECIALIST_REVIEW","ESI_CONTRACTOR_CONTROL_GAPS_SPECIALIST_REVIEW","ESI_CONTRACTOR_FACTS_MISSING","ESI_PAYMENT_CONTROLS_RECORDED_SPECIALIST_REVIEW","ESI_PAYMENT_CONTROL_GAPS_SPECIALIST_REVIEW","ESI_PAYMENT_FACTS_MISSING","ESI_ACCIDENT_CONTROLS_RECORDED_SPECIALIST_REVIEW","ESI_ACCIDENT_CONTROL_GAPS_SPECIALIST_REVIEW","ESI_ACCIDENT_FACTS_MISSING"],"retrievalTerms":["corrigendum","commencement","transition"],"text":"The controlled corrigendum remains attached to commencement context so the original notification is not represented in isolation. Its legal effect remains subject to specialist review.","contentSha256":"d3f8a2396ff5d015073cb292ef94293b5c06bfded9fb116a7a63196ee3544dd8"}]}